    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "PAA\nConquest\nof the Pacific\nJuLy 1940\nRETURN FLIGHT FROM CANTON ISLAND\nAAMIC FiGuE\nCANTON ISHAND, ONE OF THE PHOENIL ISLANDS, BE A TINY (3.5 SO MI\nATOLL LOCATED 2000 MI SOUTHWEST OF HAWAL. CLAIMED BVTHE LS. IN 185G,\nIT WAS ALSO CLAIMED, AND OCCUPIED, IM 1937 BY THE BRITISH. IN 1939, THO\nTWO COUNTRIES AGREED TO VOINT CONTROL FOR A PERIOD OF SO YEARS.\nPan American Airways' Boeing 314 NC18603 Yankee Clipper. This aircraft opened the\nvorld's first transatlantic scheduled air mail service by heavier-than-air craft, on 20\nMay, 1939. (Pan American World Airways)",
      "FIG-65.0\nGOLDEN GATE\nINTERNATIONAL\nEXPOSITION\n1940",
